 README.md  | 27 ++++++++-------------------
 src/lib.rs |  7 +------
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 25 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index cee20fb..5276407 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-# mlmorph
+# mlmorph-rs
 
 A Rust implementation of the Malayalam Morphological Analyzer using Finite State Transducer technology.
 
@@ -31,22 +31,16 @@ Add this to your `Cargo.toml`:
 
 ```toml
 [dependencies]
-mlmorph = "0.1.0"
+mlmorph = { package = "mlmorph-rs", version = "1.4.3", default-features = false }
 ```
 
 ### As a CLI Tool
 
 ```bash
-cargo install mlmorph
+cargo install mlmorph-rs
 ```
 
-Or build from source:
-
-```bash
-git clone https://github.com/smc/mlmorph
-cd mlmorph/rust
-cargo build --release
-```
+The optional `cli` feature is enabled by default and installs the `mlmorph` binary. This package embeds a pure-Rust lookup generated from SMC’s MIT grammar; SFST is a build tool only. Runtime use needs no C++ library, SFST installation, or temporary files.
 
 ## Usage
 
@@ -248,17 +242,12 @@ pub fn check_foreign_word(word: &str) -> i32;
 
 ## Requirements
 
-- **SFST Data**: The library requires the compiled Malayalam FST file (`data/malayalam.a`)
-- **Rust**: Version 1.70 or higher
+- **Data**: The compiled lookup is embedded in the crate.
+- **Rust**: Version 1.85 or higher
 
 ## Performance
 
-The Rust implementation provides significant performance improvements over the Python version:
-
-- **Analysis**: ~10x faster than Python implementation
-- **Generation**: ~8x faster than Python implementation
-- **Memory**: Lower memory footprint
-- **Concurrency**: Safe for concurrent use across threads
+Performance and full-corpus parity are measured by the enclosing mlmorph-rs build pipeline.
 
 ## Compatibility
 
@@ -270,7 +259,7 @@ Contributions are welcome! Please see the main [mlmorph project](https://gitlab.
 
